## 8. Observability

- **Structured logs**: every plugin process's stdout/stderr is captured by the host, tagged with `pluginId`, `version`, `pid`, shipped to the same log pipeline as the host — teams don't need their own logging infra.
- **Metrics** (host-side, per plugin): call count/latency/error-rate per RPC method, process memory/CPU vs. limit, restart count, circuit-breaker trips. Exposed as standard `plugin_*` Prometheus metrics so all 5 teams get dashboards for free without instrumenting anything themselves.
- **Tracing**: `traceId` propagated through the RPC envelope (§5) so a report-generation trace spans host code and every plugin it called, visible as one trace in whatever tracing backend the host already uses.
- **Health endpoint**: admin UI shows live state machine state (§4) per plugin, last health check, last crash reason, current granted permissions vs. requested — one screen to answer "why is this plugin not running."

